+# Q3 2026 Operating Brief
+
+## Executive summary
+
+Q3 was a solid quarter financially, with $720,000 in revenue against $464,000 in
+spend, leaving an operating surplus of $256,000. Support handled a heavy ticket
+load (1,250 opened) and closed the large majority of them, though the close
+rate came in below the level reported on the support dashboard. The delivery
+plan is on track, with a small schedule slip against the originally reported
+launch date once business-day math (including the mid-quarter company holiday)
+is applied. Security had a strong quarter, resolving 95.0% of detected
+incidents. Several source packets contain summary figures that do not match
+their own underlying data; these are called out below for leadership
+awareness.
+
+## Key figures
+
+| Metric | Value |
+|---|---:|
+| Q3 revenue | $720,000 |
+| Q3 spend | $464,000 |
+| Operating surplus | $256,000 |
+| Support close rate | 93.7% |
+| Launch date | 2026-10-23 |
+| Security resolution rate | 95.0% |
+
+## Notes
+
+- **Finance packet discrepancy:** the packet states total Q3 spend as
+  $463,250, but the listed spend categories (Payroll $286,400 +
+  Infrastructure $81,750 + Contractors $64,200 + Facilities $31,650) sum to
+  $464,000. The figures above use the recomputed total; finance should
+  reconcile the $750 gap.
+- **Support packet discrepancy:** the packet labels the close rate as 96.4%,
+  but 1,171 closed of 1,250 opened computes to 93.7%. Worth confirming
+  which tickets the dashboard's 96.4% figure is based on.
+- **Delivery packet discrepancy:** the packet reports a launch date of
+  2026-10-22, but summing the phase durations (Discovery 3, Build 6, QA 4,
+  Release 1 business days) from the 2026-10-05 start, skipping weekends and
+  the 2026-10-12 company holiday, puts the Release phase completion — and
+  therefore launch — on 2026-10-23. The 2026-10-22 date reported appears to
+  mark the end of QA rather than Release.
+- **Security packet:** the reported 95.0% resolution rate (76 of 80 incidents
+  resolved) checks out against the underlying data with no discrepancy.
